WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.060
London-born actor Robert Pattinson skyrocketed
to fame with the massively popular Twilight

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.290
series — and he recently made headlines
when it was announced he'd be playing the

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.980
titular role in The Batman.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.020
"And…?"

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.330
From modeling gigs to his sometimes dramatic
love life, here’s everything you need to

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.000
know about Robert Pattinson.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.839
After honing his craft in several theater
productions, Robert Pattinson landed his first

00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:28.349
big break at the age of 17: He was cast as
Cedric Diggory in the 2005 film Harry Potter

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:29.400
and the Goblet of Fire.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.020
"For a moment there, I thought you were gonna
let him get me."

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.780
He chose playing Cedric over attending university,
and the film took his acting career to a whole

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.320
new level.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.140
His performance was widely praised, and numerous
publications hailed him as "the next Jude

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.420
Law," a label that proved difficult to shake.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.839
In a 2008 interview with the BBC, Pattinson
was asked whether he agreed with that assessment,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:52.560
and he replied:

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.440
"No.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.480
[...] You get a bit of heat and everybody
says you're this, you're that.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.499
Then it dies down.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.320
You just do jobs.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.260
I don't know any actor who's followed through,
when they say he's the next this and then

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:04.280
he actually has become the next that.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.000
I don't get that.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.300
I don't see what the point is."

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:11.470
The fourth Harry Potter film put Robert Pattinson
on the map, but Twilight turned him into a

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.380
household name.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.300
Pattison landed the role of Edward Cullen
in a rather roundabout way: He was in Los

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.780
Angeles auditioning for a role he assumed
was already in the bag — and wound up bombing

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:22.500
that audition.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.120
In 2017, he told W magazine:

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.860
"The next day, it was the Twilight audition,
and I think I was at such a kind of nothing-

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.300
to-lose state, it was quite easy for me to
do."

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:38.860
And so he was cast as an unusually sensitive
vampire who falls in love with a young woman

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.060
named Bella, portrayed by Kristen Stewart.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:45.560
The role earned him legions of fans — many
of them teenage girls — but that didn't

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.250
stop him from mocking the Twilight franchise
in interviews.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.979
"My entire performance was based on having
extreme discomfort having contact lenses in

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.109
your eyes, just like…

00:01:54.109 --> 00:01:54.740
It's kinda like that."

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:59.180
"If Edward was not a fictional character,
and you met him in reality, you know, he's

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.480
one of those guys, he'd be an axe murderer."

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:04.620
He also wasn't opposed to mocking Stephenie
Meyer, the author of the Twilight novels.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:10.420
"I was convinced that Stephanie was convinced
she was Bella.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.800
And it was, like, a book that wasn't supposed
to be published."

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.880
It sounds like Pattinson has softened his
stance in recent years.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.700
In April 2019, he told USA Today:

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.730
"It's lovely now that the mania is not so
intense.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.900
[...] Now the intensity has died down and
it's just very warm memories."

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.400
In May 2019, it was announced that Robert
Pattinson would play a young incarnation of

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.260
a certain brooding superhero in The Batman,
a film that's set to premiere in 2021.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:42.220
Rather predictably, the news sent the Twitterverse
into a frenzy, and not everyone was onboard

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:42.920
with the idea.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.100
One user wrote,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.940
"I've never been so disappointed in a #Batman
casting, #RobertPattinson is a horrible choice

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.860
to play the character."

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.160
Film critic Mike McGranaghan was clearly torn
by the casting choice, tweeting:

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.280
"I honestly don't know how to feel about Robert
Pattinson as Batman.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.880
On one hand, I hate the idea, because I can't
even remotely picture him as the Dark Knight.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.700
On the other hand, I absolutely love the idea
for the exact same reason."

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.960
Meanwhile, Jimmy Kimmel offered this particularly
hot take:

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:12.700
"If you think about it, it makes sense: He
was a vampire, now he's a bat."

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.280
In 2012, Robert Pattinson's relationship with
Kristen Stewart turned him into irresistible

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.300
tabloid fodder.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:24.940
Though they tried to keep the relationship
under wraps, they were forced to come clean

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.100
in the wake of a highly publicized scandal.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:31.280
Stewart finally acknowledged their relationship
after she was photographed being intimate

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.260
with then-married director Rupert Sanders,
who worked with Stewart on Snow White and

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:35.760
the Huntsman.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.220
"When a famous actress gets caught cheating
by the paparazzi and then makes a very public

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:45.640
apology, it's no surprise that people everywhere
are reacting with 140-characters or less."

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.960
Stewart profusely apologized in a public statement,
writing:

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.690
"This momentary indiscretion has jeopardized
the most important thing in my life, the person

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:55.720
I love and respect the most, Rob.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.160
I love him, I love him, I'm so sorry."

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.940
Stewart and Pattinson briefly got back together
after the scandal, but they split for good

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.060
in 2013.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:09.240
In 2019, Pattinson suggested that he's on
good terms with Stewart, so perhaps this story

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.720
has a happy ending after all.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.660
With his chiseled features, it's not terribly
surprising that Robert Pattinson would try

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.800
his hand at modeling.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.060
He told Closer magazine that he left the industry
after four years at the age of 16, explaining:

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:26.840
"When I first started I was quite tall and
looked like a girl, so I got lots of jobs,

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.800
because it was during that period where the
androgynous look was cool.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.740
Then, I guess, I became too much of a guy,
so I never got any more jobs.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.140
I had the most unsuccessful modelling career."

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:41.390
In 2010, at the height of Twilight fever,
Pattinson was reportedly offered a huge contract

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.169
with Burberry, but he didn't take it.

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:44.540
A source told the Mirror:

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.960
"They went to ­Robert but he ­immediately,
politely, turned them down.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.420
As far as Robert sees things he’s an actor
by trade and that’s his art.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.760
He doesn’t want to start becoming a brand
or anything."

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.100
If that's true, Pattinson obviously had a
change of heart just a few short years later.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:02.980
In 2013, he became the face of Dior Homme,
and he's been working with the brand ever

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:03.480
since.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.580
As it turns out, Jude Law was the face of
Dior Homme just a few years prior — which

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.880
means Robert Pattinson became "the next Jude
Law" after all.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.140
"What's he got, better than me?!"

